<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_HogaanCoachingConversation" targetNamespace="http://hogaan.app/processes" exporter="Hogaan Process Specification" exporterVersion="1.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.9.0">
  <bpmn:message id="Message_Inbound" name="InboundUserMessageReceived" />
  <bpmn:signal id="Signal_SessionClose" name="SessionCloseTrigger" />
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Hogaan_Coaching">
    <bpmn:documentation>Collaboration scope for Coaching Conversation. Single pool ('Hogaan Coaching Platform') uses ALL FIVE lanes — this is the most lane-comprehensive of all six processes. WhatsApp Gateway hosts delivery and opt-out replies; Orchestration Engine hosts the spine and parallel gateways; LLM Service hosts intent classifier, main LLM call, fallbacks, meta and clarify generators; Data Layer hosts the parallel context fetch (Step 5) and parallel post-turn persistence (Step 12); External Services hosts Crisis and Incident handling.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Hogaan" name="Hogaan Coaching Platform" processRef="Process_CoachingConversation" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_CoachingConversation" name="Hogaan Coaching Conversation Process" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Hogaan Coaching Conversation Process. The PRIMARY user-facing process — every inbound user message after onboarding is handled here. Orchestrates intent classification, context retrieval, prompt assembly, LLM response generation, quality validation, WhatsApp delivery, and post-turn persistence in a single ~6-second turn.

DESIGN PRINCIPLES:

(1) CRISIS DETECTION IS NON-NEGOTIABLE AND BYPASSES EVERYTHING.
Step 1 includes a high-recall crisis classifier. If crisis is detected at triage, the message routes IMMEDIATELY to Call_CrisisSub — bypassing intent classification, context retrieval, prompt assembly, LLM call, and delivery. The user is never given a coaching response when they need crisis resources. A SECOND crisis check happens at Step 10 (Response Quality Check) — if the QA process detects crisis content in the LLM-generated response (e.g., user expressed crisis content within the message and our LLM didn't catch it), routing diverts to Crisis even after the response was generated.

(2) PARALLEL CONTEXT FETCH IS BLOCKING (Step 5).
The Step 5 parallel gateways are blocking — Step 6 cannot proceed until ALL three context branches (memory, profile, recent session) have returned. This is critical for response quality. The branches run in parallel for latency (target: ~200ms total) but the join is hard.

(3) PARALLEL POST-TURN PERSISTENCE IS FAIL-OPEN (Step 12).
The Step 12 parallel gateways are fail-OPEN — if any of the four post-turn tasks (log, memory write, metrics, pattern detection) fails, the failure routes to Call_Incident_PostTurn (asynchronous incident logging) and the join still completes. The user already received their response at Step 11; post-turn persistence failures do NOT degrade the user experience. This contrasts with Step 5 where failures DO matter (they degrade the response quality).

(4) INTENT ROUTING SHORT-CIRCUITS NON-COACHING REQUESTS.
Step 4 routes 4 intent classes:
- Coaching (default) → continue full pipeline through LLM
- ScenarioRequest → Call_ScenarioSub → E4 (the scenario subprocess handles its own delivery)
- ProfileUpdate → Call_ProfileSub → E5 (profile subprocess handles its own delivery)
- MetaQuestion → Task_MetaResponse → E6 (meta response is a templated answer about the system)

These short-circuits avoid unnecessary LLM cost and latency for non-coaching turns.

(5) LLM ERROR HANDLING IS CATEGORIZED.
Step 9 has FOUR distinct error boundary events (Timeout, RateLimit, ContentFilter, ServiceUnavailable) with three different fallback strategies:
- Timeout / RateLimit → Task_Fallback_FastModel (try a quicker, less capable model)
- ContentFilter → Task_Fallback_SafeResponse (templated safe-content message; do NOT try another model)
- ServiceUnavailable → directly to E11 (no fallback worth attempting; caller knows infra is down)

Both fallback paths converge with the normal-success path at Gateway_LLM_Merge before quality check.

(6) LATENCY BUDGET (~6000ms total turn time):
- Step 1 Validation + Triage: 50ms
- Step 2 Session State: 30ms
- Step 3 Intent Classifier (LLM): 300ms (optimized model)
- Step 5 Context Fetch (parallel): 250ms (longest of 3)
- Step 6-7 Tagging + Clarification: 30ms
- Step 8 Prompt Assembly: 60ms
- Step 9 LLM Generation: 5000ms hard cap (typical p50 ~2000ms)
- Step 10 QA (Response Quality Check): 500ms
- Step 11 WhatsApp Delivery: 200ms
- Step 12 Post-turn (fire and forget): 0ms blocking
- Step 13 Continuation Decision: 5ms

OWNERSHIP: Orchestration Engine runs the process spine, all gateways (including 4 parallel gateways), business rule tasks, and the call activities to other in-platform processes (Session Lifecycle, Prompt Assembly, RQC, Scenario, Profile). LLM Service hosts the intent classifier, the main LLM call with all four error boundaries, both fallback tasks, the meta response generation, and the clarifying question generation. Data Layer hosts the three Step 5 context-fetch tasks and the four Step 12 post-turn persistence tasks. WhatsApp Gateway hosts the delivery call activity (to Process #11) and the two opt-out reply tasks (Handle Media, Handle Reject). External Services hosts the Crisis Handoff and Incident Handling call activities.

ENGINE TARGET: This artifact is a SPECIFICATION not a deployment. isExecutable=false. Use as the source-of-truth functional spec for service implementation.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Coaching">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_WhatsAppGateway" name="WhatsApp Gateway">
        <bpmn:documentation>WhatsApp Gateway. Hosts the message-delivery call activity (Step 11, invoking Process #11), and the two early-exit opt-out reply tasks: Task_Handle_Media for unsupported media types and Task_Handle_Reject for content-policy violations.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Step11_Delivery</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Handle_Media</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Handle_Reject</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E8_MediaReject</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E9_MessageReject</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_OrchestrationEngine" name="Orchestration Engine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Orchestration Engine. Hosts the entire process spine: start event, Step 1 validation/triage with embedded crisis classifier, all decision gateways (5-way triage, 4-way intent router, clarify, LLM merge, QA outcome, close), both Step 5 blocking parallel gateways, both Step 12 fail-open parallel gateways, Step 13 continuation, Event_SignalClose, all 12 end events, and call activities to in-platform Hogaan processes (Session Lifecycle, Prompt Assembly, RQC, Scenario, Profile).</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_MessageReceived</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step1_Validation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step1_Triage</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Step2_Session</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step5_ContextSplit</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step5_ContextJoin</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step6_PreTagging</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step7_ClarificationDecision</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step7_Clarify</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Step8_Prompt</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_LLM_Merge</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Step10_QA</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step10_Outcome</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step12_PostSplit</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step12_PostJoin</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step13_Continuation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Step13_Close</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_SignalClose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_ScenarioSub</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_ProfileSub</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E1_TurnCompleted</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E2_TurnCompletedSessionClosed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E3_DegradedQuality</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E4_ScenarioHandoff</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E5_ProfileAck</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E6_MetaResponse</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E10_Clarify</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E11_Unavailable</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E12_SilentDrop</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_LLMService" name="LLM Service">
        <bpmn:documentation>LLM Service. Hosts every task that calls a language model: Step 3 intent classifier (small/optimized model), Step 9 main response generation (primary LLM with 5000ms hard cap and 4 categorized error boundaries), Task_Fallback_FastModel (quicker/less capable model for timeout and rate-limit recovery), Task_Fallback_SafeResponse (templated safe-content response for content-filter recovery — does not actually call an LLM but lives here for cohesion with the LLM error-handling path), Task_MetaResponse (templated answer to system-about questions), Task_ClarifyingGen (LLM call to produce a focused clarifying question when ambiguity is detected).</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step3_Intent</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step9_LLM</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Error_LLM_Timeout</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Error_LLM_RateLimit</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Error_LLM_Unavailable</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Error_LLM_Filter</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Fallback_FastModel</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Fallback_SafeResponse</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_MetaResponse</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ClarifyingGen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_DataLayer" name="Data Layer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Data Layer. Hosts every task that reads from or writes to persistent storage: Step 5a Memory Retrieval (call activity to Process #8 Memory Read — vector store), Step 5b User Profile Fetch (DB read), Step 5c Recent Session Context (cache read), and the four Step 12 post-turn persistence tasks (Conversation Turn Log, Memory Write call activity to Process #8, Metrics Emission, Profile Pattern Detection). All four post-turn tasks have boundary error events catching write failures and routing to incident handling.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Step5a_Memory</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step5b_Profile</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step5c_Context</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step12a_Log</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Step12b_MemoryWrite</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step12c_Metrics</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step12d_Pattern</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Boundary_12a</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Boundary_12b</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Boundary_12c</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Boundary_12d</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_ExternalServices" name="External Services">
        <bpmn:documentation>External Services. Hosts the Crisis Handoff Subprocess (handles user crisis escalation — provides crisis resources, alerts on-call, escalates to human responder where applicable) and the Incident Handling call activity (asynchronous post-turn for any persistence failures from Step 12 branches). Both processes route to operational systems outside the in-platform Hogaan core.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_CrisisSub</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Incident_PostTurn</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_End_E7_Crisis</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_InboundMessage" name="InboundMessage" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_InboundMessage" name="InboundMessage" dataObjectRef="DO_InboundMessage">
      <bpmn:documentation>InboundMessage — the trigger payload from the WhatsApp Gateway webhook. Fields: userId (resolved by Process #12 before this process is invoked), phoneNumberHash, messageText, mediaReferences (if any), inboundMessageId, receivedAt, sessionContextHints (if known from caller).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_SessionContext" name="SessionContext" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_SessionContext" name="SessionContext" dataObjectRef="DO_SessionContext">
      <bpmn:documentation>SessionContext — output of Step 2 (Session State Resolution from Process #6). Fields: sessionId, isNewSession (boolean), turnCount within session, lastTurnAt, sessionMetadata. Used downstream for continuation decision and metrics.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_UserProfile" name="UserProfileSnapshot" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_UserProfile" name="UserProfileSnapshot" dataObjectRef="DO_UserProfile">
      <bpmn:documentation>UserProfileSnapshot — output of Step 5b. The user's persistent coaching-relevant attributes loaded into memory for this turn: goals (mapped to 12 Practices), role (Student | Professional | Leader), location, isDiaspora, mappedPractices array, tenureInPlatform, profileFlags. Used for personalization and tag pre-tagging.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_RetrievedMemories" name="RetrievedMemories" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_RetrievedMemories" name="RetrievedMemories" dataObjectRef="DO_RetrievedMemories">
      <bpmn:documentation>RetrievedMemories — output of Step 5a (Memory Retrieval from Process #8). Top-N relevant memory entries from the user's vector store, scored by semantic similarity to the current message. Each entry: memoryId, content, originalTurnAt, similarity score, topics. Used by Step 8 Prompt Assembly to provide long-term context.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_Tags" name="PracticeAndLevelTags" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_Tags" name="PracticeAndLevelTags" dataObjectRef="DO_Tags">
      <bpmn:documentation>PracticeAndLevelTags — output of Step 6 (Pre-Tagging). Fields: practiceTag (one of Hamse's 12 Practices), levelTag (one of 4 Levels: Self/Team/Organization/Community), tagSource (rule-based | profile-default | message-explicit), tagConfidence. Used by Step 8 Prompt Assembly to anchor the response in the right practice.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_Prompt" name="AssembledPrompt" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_Prompt" name="AssembledPrompt" dataObjectRef="DO_Prompt">
      <bpmn:documentation>AssembledPrompt — output of Step 8 (Prompt Assembly call to Process #9). The full prompt string ready for LLM call, plus metadata: responseMode, determinismHash, libraryVersionsUsed, degradationFlags, tokenCount.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_CandidateResp" name="CandidateResponse" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_CandidateResp" name="CandidateResponse" dataObjectRef="DO_CandidateResp">
      <bpmn:documentation>CandidateResponse — raw LLM output from Step 9 (or from a fallback path). Fields: rawText, modelUsed, latencyMs, tokenUsage. Goes into Step 10 QA for validation.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_ApprovedResp" name="ApprovedResponse" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_ApprovedResp" name="ApprovedResponse" dataObjectRef="DO_ApprovedResp">
      <bpmn:documentation>ApprovedResponse — output of Step 10 (Response Quality Check). The candidate response that passed QA (or a regenerated/fallback variant chosen by RQC). Ready for delivery to the user.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DO_Delivery" name="DeliveryReceipt" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DOR_Delivery" name="DeliveryReceipt" dataObjectRef="DO_Delivery">
      <bpmn:documentation>DeliveryReceipt — output of Step 11 (WhatsApp Message Delivery call to Process #11). Fields: waMessageId, dispatchedAt, dispatchPathTaken (E1 normal | E2 retry | E3 queued from Process #11). Used by Step 12 logging.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_MessageReceived" name="Inbound User Message Received">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process trigger. Fired by the WhatsApp Gateway when an inbound message arrives from a user who has been resolved by Process #12 (User Auth &amp; Identity) and identified as an onboarded user (status=='onboarded').

EVENT TYPE: Message start event. PAYLOAD: see DOR_InboundMessage. The trigger is correlated by userId.

UPSTREAM CHAIN: WA Gateway webhook → Process #12 (Identity) → returns userId+status → if status==onboarded, this process is invoked. If status in [onboarding_started, dormant], Process #1 (Onboarding) is invoked instead.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Start_To_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MsgDef_Inbound" messageRef="Message_Inbound" />
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step1_Validation" name="Step 1: Validation, Triage &#38; Crisis Detection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 1 — Message Validation, Triage, and Crisis Detection.

PURPOSE: First-line validation, triage, and the critical high-recall crisis check.

CHECKS (in order):
1. Empty/whitespace-only message → validationStatus='Empty' → silent drop at E12
2. Media-only message (image/video/audio with no text) → validationStatus='Media' → friendly reply that media isn't supported yet
3. Crisis keywords/patterns (high-recall classifier — favors false positives over false negatives): direct mentions of self-harm, suicide, urgent danger, abuse → validationStatus='Crisis' → IMMEDIATELY route to Crisis Handoff (does NOT proceed to LLM)
4. Content policy violations (abuse, spam, prohibited topics) → validationStatus='Reject'
5. Otherwise → validationStatus='Valid' → continue pipeline

CRISIS CLASSIFIER NOTES: Implementation should err HEAVILY on the side of recall. False positives (sending crisis resources to a user who isn't in crisis) are acceptable; false negatives (missing a real crisis) are catastrophic. The classifier may be a small fine-tuned model OR rule-based with a curated keyword/pattern catalog. Both approaches are acceptable; the choice is an implementation detail. The catalog is maintained by Process #17 with regional variants for Somali speakers.

OUTPUT: validationStatus enum.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Business rule task. ~50ms total budget including crisis classifier.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Start_To_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1_To_GW1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Step1_Triage" name="Triage Outcome" default="Flow_Triage_Valid">
      <bpmn:documentation>5-way triage routing based on validation outcome.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- VALID branch (default): validationStatus == 'Valid' → proceed to Step 2 (Session State)
- CRISIS branch: validationStatus == 'Crisis' → IMMEDIATELY route to Call_CrisisSub (bypassing all coaching pipeline)
- MEDIA branch: validationStatus == 'Media' → route to Task_Handle_Media (send friendly reply, terminate at E8)
- REJECT branch: validationStatus == 'Reject' → route to Task_Handle_Reject (send rejection notice, log incident, terminate at E9)
- EMPTY branch: validationStatus == 'Empty' → silent drop at E12 (no reply sent)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1_To_GW1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Triage_Valid</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Triage_Crisis</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Triage_Media</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Triage_Reject</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Triage_Silent</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E12_SilentDrop" name="E12: Silent Drop">
      <bpmn:documentation>E12: SilentDrop. Empty/whitespace-only message received; no reply sent. The empty message is logged for analytics but the user receives nothing.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Triage_Silent</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Handle_Media" name="Handle Media (Send Reply)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Handle media-only message (no text).

PURPOSE: Send a friendly reply explaining that media files aren't supported yet (MVP constraint), and invite the user to send text instead.

MESSAGE CONTENT (Hamse voice): 'I can't process images, audio, or video yet — just text for now. Tell me what's on your mind.'

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task that sends via Process #11. Lives in WhatsApp Gateway lane.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Triage_Media</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Media_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E8_MediaReject" name="E8: Media Not Supported">
      <bpmn:documentation>E8: MediaNotSupported. User sent media-only message; friendly reply sent explaining text-only constraint.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Media_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Handle_Reject" name="Handle Rejection (Send Notice)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Handle policy-rejected message.

PURPOSE: Send a brief rejection notice when the message violated content policy (abuse, spam, prohibited topics). Log incident at moderate severity.

MESSAGE CONTENT: 'I can't help with that. Let's keep things constructive — what's on your mind that I can actually help with?'

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task that sends via Process #11 and logs an incident. Lives in WhatsApp Gateway lane. NOTE: this is the path that Gemini's original BPMN had broken (Reject was wired to the same handler as Media, terminating at E8 instead of E9). This rebuild splits them so E9 is properly used.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Triage_Reject</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Reject_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E9_MessageReject" name="E9: Message Rejected">
      <bpmn:documentation>E9: MessageRejected. User's message violated content policy; rejection notice sent and incident logged. Repeat offenders may be added to the suppression list.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Reject_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Step2_Session" name="Step 2: Session State Resolution" calledElement="Process_SessionLifecycle">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 2 — Session State Resolution.

PURPOSE: Determine session continuity. Either continue an open session or start a new one.

LOGIC: Call Process #6 (Session Lifecycle) with userId. Returns sessionId (existing or newly created), isNewSession flag, turnCount within session, lastTurnAt, sessionMetadata.

OUTPUT: sessionContext populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity invoking Process #6. ~30ms latency budget.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Triage_Valid</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2_To_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step3_Intent" name="Step 3: Intent Classification">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 3 — Intent Classification (LLM-based).

PURPOSE: Classify the user's message into one of 8 intent classes to drive routing.

INTENT CLASSES:
- Coaching (the default — most messages): the user is bringing a leadership challenge, situation, or question
- ScenarioRequest: the user is asking for or about a coaching scenario / role-play exercise
- ProfileUpdate: the user is updating their profile attributes (e.g., "I just got promoted to Director")
- MetaQuestion: the user is asking about the system itself ("what can you help me with", "who built you")
- Greeting: simple "hi", "hello" with no substantive content (handled as Coaching by default)
- Affirmation: "yes", "ok", "thanks" — context-dependent (handled as Coaching for context preservation)
- ClarificationResponse: response to a prior clarifying question from us (handled as Coaching, picks up prior context)
- OutOfScope: clearly off-topic (politics, asking for code, etc.) — handled as Coaching with a polite redirect

LOGIC: LLM classifier call with optimized small model. Returns intent label and confidence score.

OUTPUT: intent enum.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task calling a small LLM (e.g., Anthropic's smallest tier) with a structured-output schema. ~300ms latency budget. CRITICAL: this is on every turn so latency matters more than absolute accuracy.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2_To_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3_To_GW2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter" name="Intent Router" default="Flow_Intent_Coaching">
      <bpmn:documentation>4-way intent routing.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- COACHING branch (default): intent in [Coaching, Greeting, Affirmation, ClarificationResponse, OutOfScope] → continue to Step 5 (Context Fetch)
- SCENARIO branch: intent == 'ScenarioRequest' → route to Call_ScenarioSub which handles its own delivery, terminates at E4
- PROFILE branch: intent == 'ProfileUpdate' → route to Call_ProfileSub which handles its own delivery, terminates at E5
- META branch: intent == 'MetaQuestion' → route to Task_MetaResponse (templated answer), terminates at E6

The 3 short-circuit branches avoid invoking the full LLM coaching pipeline for non-coaching requests, saving cost and latency.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3_To_GW2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Intent_Coaching</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Intent_Scenario</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Intent_Profile</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Intent_Meta</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_ScenarioSub" name="Scenario Learning Subprocess" calledElement="Process_Scenario">
      <bpmn:documentation>Scenario Learning Subprocess.

PURPOSE: Handle scenario-based learning requests (role-plays, structured exercises, situational learning).

LOGIC: Call activity to scenario subprocess (likely Process #5 or similar). The subprocess handles its own delivery — this process terminates at E4 once the call returns.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Intent_Scenario</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Scenario_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E4_ScenarioHandoff" name="E4: Scenario Handoff">
      <bpmn:documentation>E4: ScenarioHandoff. Scenario subprocess took over the turn. This process exits cleanly without further action.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Scenario_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_ProfileSub" name="Profile Update Subprocess" calledElement="Process_ProfileUpdate">
      <bpmn:documentation>Profile Update Subprocess.

PURPOSE: Handle explicit profile-update requests from the user (e.g., "I just changed jobs", "I'm now leading a team of 10").

LOGIC: Call activity to profile-update subprocess. Updates user profile and sends acknowledgment. This process terminates at E5.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Intent_Profile</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Profile_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E5_ProfileAck" name="E5: Profile Update Ack">
      <bpmn:documentation>E5: ProfileUpdateAck. Profile was updated and acknowledgment sent. This process exits cleanly.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Profile_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_MetaResponse" name="Meta Response (Templated)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Meta Response Generator.

PURPOSE: Answer questions about the system itself ('what can you help me with', 'who built you', 'what is Hogaan'). Uses templated responses from the Voice Rules library — does NOT call the main LLM.

LOGIC: Templated answer keyed on the meta-question type, then sent via Process #11.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task with templated response and direct delivery. ~200ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Intent_Meta</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Meta_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E6_MetaResponse" name="E6: Meta Response Delivered">
      <bpmn:documentation>E6: MetaResponseDelivered. Templated meta response sent. This process exits cleanly.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Meta_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Gateway_Step5_ContextSplit" name="Split: Parallel Context Fetch (Blocking)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Parallel split for blocking context fetch. Three branches run concurrently to fetch context for the LLM call:
- Memory retrieval (semantic search of user's vector store via Process #8)
- User profile snapshot (DB read)
- Recent session context (cache read of last 3-5 turns)

PURPOSE: Reduce wall-clock latency by parallelizing 3 independent fetches. Total elapsed = max(branch_latencies) ~ 250ms; serial would be ~400ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Intent_Coaching</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Split_To_5a</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Split_To_5b</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Split_To_5c</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Step5a_Memory" name="Step 5a: Memory Retrieval" calledElement="Process_MemoryRead">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 5a — Memory Retrieval (call activity to Process #8 Read).

PURPOSE: Fetch top-N most relevant past memory entries from the user's vector store, scored against the current message.

LOGIC: Call Process #8 Memory Read with userId, currentMessageText, top_n (default 5). Process #8 returns scored results.

OUTPUT: retrievedMemories array.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. ~200ms latency budget.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Split_To_5a</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5a_To_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step5b_Profile" name="Step 5b: User Profile Fetch">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 5b — User Profile Snapshot Fetch.

PURPOSE: Load the user's persistent profile attributes for this turn.

LOGIC: Single DB read by userId. Returns goals, role, mappedPractices, location, isDiaspora, tenure, profileFlags.

OUTPUT: userProfile snapshot.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task with cached DB read. Sub-50ms (cache hit) or sub-150ms (cold).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Split_To_5b</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5b_To_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step5c_Context" name="Step 5c: Recent Session Context">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 5c — Recent Session Context Fetch.

PURPOSE: Fetch the last 3-5 turns from the session cache for short-term continuity context.

LOGIC: Cache (Redis) read keyed on sessionId, returning ordered list of recent turns.

OUTPUT: sessionTurns array.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task with Redis read. Sub-20ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Split_To_5c</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5c_To_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Gateway_Step5_ContextJoin" name="Join: All Context Branches">
      <bpmn:documentation>Parallel join for context fetch. BLOCKING — Step 6 will not proceed until all three Step 5 branches have returned. This is intentional: the LLM call requires all three context blocks to produce a quality response.

NOTE: Failures within any branch are NOT modeled here as causing flow termination. In implementation, individual branch failures should fall back to empty context for that branch (e.g., empty memories list, default profile fields, empty session turns) so the join still completes. This is a pragmatic choice — partial context is better than no response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5a_To_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5b_To_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5c_To_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Join_To_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step6_PreTagging" name="Step 6: Practice &#38; Level Pre-Tagging">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 6 — Practice and Level Pre-Tagging.

PURPOSE: Anchor the upcoming LLM response in 1 of Hamse's 12 Practices and 1 of 4 Levels, based on the user's intent, profile, and current message.

LOGIC: Rule-based mapping using:
- Profile-default tags (from user.mappedPractices)
- Message-explicit signals (e.g., user mentions "team conflict" → Empathy/Team)
- Intent-aware overrides (e.g., explicit reference to a practice the user is working on)

The tags are passed to Step 8 Prompt Assembly to ensure the response is structurally anchored in the framework — preventing generic motivational fluff.

OUTPUT: tags = { practiceTag, levelTag, tagSource, tagConfidence }.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Business rule task with deterministic DMN logic. ~15ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Join_To_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6_To_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step7_ClarificationDecision" name="Step 7: Clarification Decision">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 7 — Clarification Decision.

PURPOSE: Decide whether to ask the user a clarifying question instead of attempting a coaching response now.

AMBIGUITY TRIGGERS:
- Message is too short or too vague to coach on (e.g., "I have a problem")
- Message references multiple distinct issues — coaching all of them at once would dilute quality
- Message contains a question we can't answer well without more context
- Confidence in tag classification is low

LOGIC: Rule-based scoring against ambiguity triggers. Above a threshold → recommend clarification.

OUTPUT: needsClarification (boolean), clarificationFocus (which axis is ambiguous).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Business rule task. ~10ms. CRITICAL TRADE-OFF: better to ask one good clarifying question than ship a generic coaching response. Lean toward 'clarify' when in doubt.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6_To_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_7_To_GW3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Step7_Clarify" name="Needs Clarification?" default="Flow_Clarify_No">
      <bpmn:documentation>Routes based on clarification decision.

DECISION LOGIC:
- NO branch (default): needsClarification == false → proceed to Step 8 (Prompt Assembly)
- YES branch: needsClarification == true → route to Task_ClarifyingGen which generates a focused clarifying question and terminates at E10</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_7_To_GW3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Clarify_No</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Clarify_Yes</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ClarifyingGen" name="Generate Clarifying Question (LLM)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Generate Clarifying Question.

PURPOSE: When Step 7 decides clarification is needed, generate a focused clarifying question via LLM that targets the specific axis of ambiguity flagged by Step 7.

LOGIC: Small LLM call (or templated, depending on ambiguity type) to produce a focused question, then send via Process #11.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. ~600ms latency including delivery.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Clarify_Yes</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ClarifyGen_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E10_Clarify" name="E10: Clarifying Question Sent">
      <bpmn:documentation>E10: ClarifyingQuestionSent. We asked the user a clarifying question instead of attempting a coaching response. The user's reply will start a new turn that picks up the context.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ClarifyGen_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Step8_Prompt" name="Step 8: Prompt Assembly" calledElement="Process_PromptAssembly">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 8 — Prompt Assembly (call activity to Process #9).

PURPOSE: Assemble the deterministic prompt with system template, framing, voice rules, cultural framing (conditional), memory block, session context, profile block, and current user message.

LOGIC: Call Process #9 (Prompt Assembly) with all collected context. Returns assembled prompt + metadata.

OUTPUT: AssembledPrompt + degradationFlags + determinismHash + tokenCount.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. ~60ms latency budget.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Clarify_No</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_8_To_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step9_LLM" name="Step 9: Primary LLM Response Generation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 9 — Primary LLM Response Generation.

PURPOSE: The main coaching response generation. Calls the primary high-quality LLM with the assembled prompt.

LOGIC: HTTP call to Anthropic API (or chosen provider) with the assembled prompt. Hard timeout: 5000ms.

OUTPUT: rawText, modelUsed, latencyMs, tokenUsage.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. The 5000ms hard cap is critical — better to time out and fall back than block the user indefinitely.

ERROR BOUNDARIES (4 distinct categories):
- Timeout: 5s elapsed without response → Task_Fallback_FastModel
- RateLimit: API returned 429 → Task_Fallback_FastModel
- ContentFilter: API rejected the prompt for content reasons → Task_Fallback_SafeResponse (do NOT retry with a different model — the issue is the input)
- ServiceUnavailable: API returned 5xx or unreachable → directly to E11 (no fallback worth attempting)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_8_To_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_9_To_Merge</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Error_LLM_Timeout" name="LLM Timeout (&#62;5s)" attachedToRef="Task_Step9_LLM">
      <bpmn:documentation>Boundary timer event on Step 9. Fires if the LLM call takes longer than 5000ms. Routes to Task_Fallback_FastModel which attempts a quicker, less-capable model. Note: a successful fallback still flags the response as 'degraded' for tracking.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_Timeout</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="TimerDef_S9">
        <bpmn:timeDuration xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">PT5S</bpmn:timeDuration>
      </bpmn:timerEventDefinition>
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Error_LLM_RateLimit" name="LLM Rate Limit (429)" attachedToRef="Task_Step9_LLM">
      <bpmn:documentation>Boundary error event on Step 9. Catches 429 from the LLM API. Routes to Task_Fallback_FastModel which uses a different model (typically a smaller tier with separate rate limits).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_Rate</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Error_LLM_RateLimit" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Error_LLM_Filter" name="LLM Content Filter" attachedToRef="Task_Step9_LLM">
      <bpmn:documentation>Boundary error event on Step 9. Catches content-filter rejection from the LLM API. Routes to Task_Fallback_SafeResponse — do NOT try another model, because the issue is the prompt content, not the model. The safe response acknowledges to the user that we can't address that particular topic and offers a redirect.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_Filter</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Error_LLM_Filter" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Error_LLM_Unavailable" name="LLM Service Unavailable" attachedToRef="Task_Step9_LLM">
      <bpmn:documentation>Boundary error event on Step 9. Catches 5xx or network unreachable from the LLM API. Routes DIRECTLY to E11 — no fallback worth attempting if the entire LLM service is down. Caller is informed; engineering alerted.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_Unavailable</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Error_LLM_Unavailable" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Fallback_FastModel" name="Fallback: Fast Model">
      <bpmn:documentation>Fallback path for LLM timeout or rate-limit errors.

PURPOSE: Try a quicker, less capable model when the primary LLM is too slow or rate-limited. Most messages can still get a usable (if less polished) response from a smaller model.

LOGIC: Call to a smaller/quicker LLM tier (e.g., Anthropic's smallest model or a local model) with the same assembled prompt. Hard cap: 2000ms.

OUTPUT: candidateResponse with fallbackModel flag set.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. Response will be flagged as 'degraded' downstream so the response quality check applies stricter validation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_Timeout</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_Rate</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Fast_Merge</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Fallback_SafeResponse" name="Fallback: Safe Response">
      <bpmn:documentation>Fallback path for content-filter errors.

PURPOSE: When the LLM rejected the prompt for content-filter reasons, return a curated safe response acknowledging the topic isn't something we can address well, with a gentle redirect.

LOGIC: Templated response from the Voice Rules library (managed by Process #17). Does NOT actually call an LLM — uses a pre-approved templated answer.

OUTPUT: candidateResponse with safeResponse flag set.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task that fetches a templated string. Sub-10ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_Filter</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Safe_Merge</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_LLM_Merge" name="Merge: LLM Output">
      <bpmn:documentation>3-way merge gateway converging the normal LLM success path, fast-model fallback path, and safe-response fallback path. All three converge here before the QA step.

DECISION LOGIC: Pass-through merge. All incoming flows route to Step 10.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_9_To_Merge</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Fast_Merge</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Safe_Merge</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Merge_To_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Step10_QA" name="Step 10: Response Quality Check" calledElement="Process_ResponseQualityCheck">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 10 — Response Quality Check (call activity to Process #10).

PURPOSE: Validate the candidate response against Hogaan's brand and safety standards before delivery. The 10 quality checks include voice/tone alignment, cultural appropriateness, factual grounding, crisis content detection, and brand consistency.

LOGIC: Call Process #10 (Response Quality Check) with the candidate response and context.

OUTCOMES:
- Approved → proceed to delivery
- CrisisEscalation → diverge to Crisis (the QA process detected crisis content the LLM missed; user gets crisis resources, not a coaching response)
- ServiceUnavailable → terminate at E11 (RQC infrastructure failure)

OUTPUT: qaOutcome enum, approvedResponse (if approved).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. ~500ms latency budget. Note: regeneration loops within RQC are absorbed there (not modeled at this level).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Merge_To_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_10_To_GW4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Step10_Outcome" name="QA Outcome" default="Flow_QA_Approved">
      <bpmn:documentation>3-way QA outcome routing.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- APPROVED branch (default): qaOutcome == 'Approved' → proceed to Step 11 (Delivery)
- CRISIS branch: qaOutcome == 'CrisisEscalation' → divert to Call_CrisisSub. CRITICAL: this is the second crisis-detection point; QA caught crisis content the Step 1 classifier missed.
- UNAVAILABLE branch: qaOutcome == 'ServiceUnavailable' → terminate at E11. RQC infrastructure failure; user receives error.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_10_To_GW4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_QA_Approved</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_QA_Crisis</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_QA_Unavailable</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E11_Unavailable" name="E11: Service Unavailable">
      <bpmn:documentation>E11: ServiceUnavailable. LLM service or RQC service was unreachable. User receives error message; engineering alerted. Target: &lt;0.5% of turns.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_Unavailable</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_QA_Unavailable</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Step11_Delivery" name="Step 11: WhatsApp Message Delivery" calledElement="Process_WAMessageDelivery">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 11 — WhatsApp Message Delivery (call activity to Process #11).

PURPOSE: Push the approved response to the user via WhatsApp Business API.

LOGIC: Call Process #11 with userId, phoneNumber, messageContent (approved response), priority='High', correlationId=turnId.

OUTPUT: deliveryReceipt (waMessageId, dispatchedAt, dispatchPathTaken).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. ~200ms latency budget. Process #11 handles all the idempotency, suppression, window checking, and rate limiting; this process just hands off the payload.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_QA_Approved</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_11_To_Split</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Gateway_Step12_PostSplit" name="Split: Post-Turn Persistence (Fail-Open)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Parallel split for post-turn persistence. FAIL-OPEN — branch failures route to incident handling but do NOT block the join.

PURPOSE: After the user has received their response (Step 11 succeeded), we need to persist the turn for memory, logging, metrics, and pattern detection. These can fail without affecting the user experience, so they're parallelized for speed and run with fail-open semantics.

CONTRAST: Step 5 parallel was BLOCKING (we needed all context to make the LLM call). Step 12 parallel is FAIL-OPEN (the user already got their response; persistence is best-effort).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_11_To_Split</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Post_12a</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Post_12b</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Post_12c</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Post_12d</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step12a_Log" name="Step 12a: Conversation Turn Log">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 12a — Conversation Turn Logging.

PURPOSE: Persist the full turn record (user message, generated response, model used, tags, latency, QA outcome, delivery receipt) to the conversation log store.

LOGIC: Single DB write to conversation_log table.

OUTPUT: logEntryId.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. Sub-50ms.

ERROR BOUNDARY: Boundary_12a catches DB write failure → routes to Call_Incident_PostTurn (fail-open: incident logged, post-turn persistence continues).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Post_12a</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12a_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Step12b_MemoryWrite" name="Step 12b: Memory Write" calledElement="Process_MemoryWrite">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 12b — Memory Write (call activity to Process #8).

PURPOSE: Add this turn to the user's long-term semantic memory store for future retrieval.

LOGIC: Call Process #8 Memory Write with the turn content. Process #8 handles embedding generation, vector store insert, and indexing.

OUTPUT: memoryId.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. ~150ms.

ERROR BOUNDARY: Boundary_12b catches Process #8 failure → routes to Call_Incident_PostTurn.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Post_12b</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12b_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step12c_Metrics" name="Step 12c: Metrics Emission">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 12c — Metrics Emission.

PURPOSE: Emit observability metrics for this turn: latency breakdown by step, model used, fallback path taken (if any), tag usage, QA outcomes, etc.

LOGIC: Push metrics to monitoring system (Prometheus, Datadog, etc.) via the application's metrics client.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. Sub-10ms (metrics are async-buffered).

ERROR BOUNDARY: Boundary_12c catches metrics emission failure → routes to Call_Incident_PostTurn (low severity but should still be tracked).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Post_12c</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12c_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step12d_Pattern" name="Step 12d: Profile Pattern Detection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 12d — Profile Pattern Detection.

PURPOSE: Analyze accumulated turns for patterns that should update the user profile (e.g., user has discussed conflict-resolution scenarios 5 times → flag this as a focus area; user has switched topics frequently → adjust profile signal).

LOGIC: Read recent turn signals, apply pattern-detection rules, and conditionally update profile flags.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. ~50ms.

ERROR BOUNDARY: Boundary_12d catches DB or analysis failure → routes to Call_Incident_PostTurn.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Post_12d</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12d_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Boundary_12a" name="Persistence Failed" attachedToRef="Task_Step12a_Log">
      <bpmn:documentation>Error boundary on Conversation Turn Logging. Catches log write failure. Routes to Call_Incident_PostTurn. Fail-open: post-turn persistence continues, user is unaffected.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_12a</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Boundary_12a" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Boundary_12b" name="Persistence Failed" attachedToRef="Call_Step12b_MemoryWrite">
      <bpmn:documentation>Error boundary on Memory Write. Catches Process #8 invocation failure. Routes to incident. Fail-open.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_12b</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Boundary_12b" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Boundary_12c" name="Persistence Failed" attachedToRef="Task_Step12c_Metrics">
      <bpmn:documentation>Error boundary on Metrics Emission. Catches metrics push failure. Routes to incident. Fail-open.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_12c</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Boundary_12c" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Boundary_12d" name="Persistence Failed" attachedToRef="Task_Step12d_Pattern">
      <bpmn:documentation>Error boundary on Pattern Detection. Catches DB/analysis failure. Routes to incident. Fail-open.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_12d</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_Boundary_12d" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Incident_PostTurn" name="Incident Handling (Async)" calledElement="Process_IncidentHandling">
      <bpmn:documentation>Asynchronous Incident Handling for post-turn failures.

PURPOSE: Log post-turn persistence failures for engineering investigation. The user has already received their response, so this is async/fire-and-forget — does NOT block the join.

LOGIC: Call Process #18 (Incident Handling) with failure context (which step failed, error type, turnId).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. The output flows back to the post-turn join gateway so all branches reach the join (whether they completed normally or via incident handling).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_12a</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_12b</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_12c</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_12d</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Incident_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin" name="Join: All Post-Turn Branches">
      <bpmn:documentation>Parallel join for post-turn persistence. Reached when all four branches (or their incident-handling fallbacks) have completed.

PURPOSE: Synchronization point ensuring the turn is fully persisted (or all failures are logged) before the continuation decision.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12a_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12b_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12c_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12d_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Incident_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Join_To_13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step13_Continuation" name="Step 13: Session Continuation Decision">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 13 — Session Continuation Decision.

PURPOSE: Decide whether to keep the session open (continue with next turn when user replies) or close it.

DECISION LOGIC:
- Explicit close keywords from user ("bye", "thanks done", "talk later") → sessionAction='Close'
- Maximum turn count reached for one session (e.g., 30 turns) → 'Close'
- Long inactivity expected (e.g., evening, user's typical end of work day inferred from timezone) → 'Close'
- Otherwise → 'KeepOpen'
- Optional: degraded turn (LLM was on fallback path) → flag isDegraded=true regardless of close decision

OUTPUT: sessionAction enum, isDegraded boolean.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Business rule task. ~5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Join_To_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_13_To_GW5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Step13_Close" name="Close Session?" default="Flow_End_E1">
      <bpmn:documentation>3-way terminal routing based on session continuation outcome and degradation flag.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- DEGRADED branch: isDegraded == true → terminate at E3 (DegradedQuality); session continuation decision is overridden — degraded turns close the session by default for quality reasons.
- CLOSE branch: sessionAction == 'Close' → emit SessionClose signal then terminate at E2 (TurnCompletedSessionClosed)
- DEFAULT branch: sessionAction == 'KeepOpen' → terminate at E1 (TurnCompleted)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_13_To_GW5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_End_E1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_End_E3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_End_E2_Sig</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_CrisisSub" name="Crisis Handoff Subprocess" calledElement="Process_CrisisHandoff">
      <bpmn:documentation>Crisis Handoff Subprocess.

PURPOSE: Handle user crisis events. Reachable from TWO triggers: (1) Step 1 Crisis triage, (2) Step 10 QA Crisis outcome. The two triggers indicate different sources but the response is the same: provide crisis resources, alert on-call, escalate.

LOGIC: Call activity to a Hogaan crisis subprocess. The subprocess: (a) sends crisis resources to the user via WA, (b) logs a crisis incident at HIGH severity, (c) optionally alerts a human responder per Hamse's policy, (d) marks the user profile with a crisis flag for follow-up.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Call activity. The crisis subprocess MUST NOT fail silently — its own internal error handling routes any failures to immediate escalation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Triage_Crisis</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_QA_Crisis</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Crisis_End</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E7_Crisis" name="E7: Crisis Escalation">
      <bpmn:documentation>E7: CrisisEscalation. Crisis was detected (at Step 1 OR at Step 10 QA), crisis resources sent, on-call alerted. HIGH-severity event.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Crisis_End</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E1_TurnCompleted" name="E1: Turn Completed">
      <bpmn:documentation>E1: TurnCompleted. Standard happy path. Response delivered, session continues open. User can send another message and the session continues. Target: ~85% of turns.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_End_E1</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E3_DegradedQuality" name="E3: Degraded Quality">
      <bpmn:documentation>E3: DegradedQuality. Response delivered but on a fallback path (fast-model fallback or RQC regeneration loop). Session closed by default for quality reasons. Target: &lt;5% of turns.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_End_E3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:intermediateThrowEvent id="Event_SignalClose" name="Emit SessionClose Signal">
      <bpmn:documentation>Intermediate throw event emitting SessionCloseTrigger signal. Caught by Process #6 (Session Lifecycle) to mark the session closed in the session store.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_End_E2_Sig</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Sig_To_E2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:signalEventDefinition signalRef="Signal_SessionClose" />
    </bpmn:intermediateThrowEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_End_E2_TurnCompletedSessionClosed" name="E2: Turn Completed, Session Closed">
      <bpmn:documentation>E2: TurnCompletedSessionClosed. Response delivered AND session closed (by explicit close keyword, max turn count, or inactivity). SessionClose signal emitted to Process #6. User's next message starts a new session.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Sig_To_E2</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Start_To_1" sourceRef="Start_MessageReceived" targetRef="Task_Step1_Validation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Inbound message from onboarded user; route to validation and triage.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1_To_GW1" sourceRef="Task_Step1_Validation" targetRef="Gateway_Step1_Triage">
      <bpmn:documentation>Validation+crisis classifier output; route by validationStatus.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Triage_Valid" sourceRef="Gateway_Step1_Triage" targetRef="Call_Step2_Session">
      <bpmn:documentation>Standard message; proceed to session state resolution.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">validationStatus == 'Valid' (default)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Triage_Crisis" sourceRef="Gateway_Step1_Triage" targetRef="Call_CrisisSub">
      <bpmn:documentation>Crisis detected by Step 1 high-recall classifier; IMMEDIATELY route to Crisis Handoff. NEVER reaches LLM or coaching pipeline.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">validationStatus == 'Crisis'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Triage_Media" sourceRef="Gateway_Step1_Triage" targetRef="Task_Handle_Media">
      <bpmn:documentation>Media-only message (no text); send friendly text-only reply.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">validationStatus == 'Media'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Triage_Reject" sourceRef="Gateway_Step1_Triage" targetRef="Task_Handle_Reject">
      <bpmn:documentation>Content policy violation; send rejection notice and log incident.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">validationStatus == 'Reject'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Triage_Silent" sourceRef="Gateway_Step1_Triage" targetRef="Event_End_E12_SilentDrop">
      <bpmn:documentation>Empty/whitespace-only message; silent drop at E12 (no reply sent).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">validationStatus == 'Empty'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Media_End" sourceRef="Task_Handle_Media" targetRef="Event_End_E8_MediaReject">
      <bpmn:documentation>Media-not-supported reply sent; terminate at E8.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Reject_End" sourceRef="Task_Handle_Reject" targetRef="Event_End_E9_MessageReject">
      <bpmn:documentation>Rejection notice sent and incident logged; terminate at E9.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Crisis_End" sourceRef="Call_CrisisSub" targetRef="Event_End_E7_Crisis">
      <bpmn:documentation>Crisis subprocess completed (resources sent, on-call alerted, profile flagged); terminate at E7.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2_To_3" sourceRef="Call_Step2_Session" targetRef="Task_Step3_Intent">
      <bpmn:documentation>Session state resolved; classify intent.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3_To_GW2" sourceRef="Task_Step3_Intent" targetRef="Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter">
      <bpmn:documentation>Intent classified; route by intent class.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Intent_Coaching" sourceRef="Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter" targetRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextSplit">
      <bpmn:documentation>Coaching intent (or coaching-equivalent); proceed to context fetch.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">intent in [Coaching, Greeting, Affirmation, ClarificationResponse, OutOfScope] (default)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Intent_Scenario" sourceRef="Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter" targetRef="Call_ScenarioSub">
      <bpmn:documentation>Scenario request; route to scenario subprocess (handles its own delivery).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">intent == 'ScenarioRequest'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Intent_Profile" sourceRef="Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter" targetRef="Call_ProfileSub">
      <bpmn:documentation>Profile update request; route to profile subprocess (handles its own delivery).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">intent == 'ProfileUpdate'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Intent_Meta" sourceRef="Gateway_Step4_IntentRouter" targetRef="Task_MetaResponse">
      <bpmn:documentation>Meta question about the system; templated response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">intent == 'MetaQuestion'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Scenario_End" sourceRef="Call_ScenarioSub" targetRef="Event_End_E4_ScenarioHandoff">
      <bpmn:documentation>Scenario subprocess completed; terminate at E4.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Profile_End" sourceRef="Call_ProfileSub" targetRef="Event_End_E5_ProfileAck">
      <bpmn:documentation>Profile updated and acknowledgment sent; terminate at E5.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Meta_End" sourceRef="Task_MetaResponse" targetRef="Event_End_E6_MetaResponse">
      <bpmn:documentation>Meta response sent; terminate at E6.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Split_To_5a" sourceRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextSplit" targetRef="Call_Step5a_Memory">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 1: parallel memory retrieval from Process #8.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Split_To_5b" sourceRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextSplit" targetRef="Task_Step5b_Profile">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 2: parallel user profile fetch (DB read).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Split_To_5c" sourceRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextSplit" targetRef="Task_Step5c_Context">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 3: parallel recent session context fetch (cache read).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5a_To_Join" sourceRef="Call_Step5a_Memory" targetRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Memory retrieval complete; converge at parallel join.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5b_To_Join" sourceRef="Task_Step5b_Profile" targetRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Profile fetched; converge.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5c_To_Join" sourceRef="Task_Step5c_Context" targetRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Session context fetched; converge.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Join_To_6" sourceRef="Gateway_Step5_ContextJoin" targetRef="Task_Step6_PreTagging">
      <bpmn:documentation>All 3 context branches complete; pre-tag practice and level.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6_To_7" sourceRef="Task_Step6_PreTagging" targetRef="Task_Step7_ClarificationDecision">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tags assigned; check if clarification is needed.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_7_To_GW3" sourceRef="Task_Step7_ClarificationDecision" targetRef="Gateway_Step7_Clarify">
      <bpmn:documentation>Clarification decision; route by needsClarification.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Clarify_No" sourceRef="Gateway_Step7_Clarify" targetRef="Call_Step8_Prompt">
      <bpmn:documentation>Message is clear enough; proceed to prompt assembly.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">needsClarification == false (default)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Clarify_Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_Step7_Clarify" targetRef="Task_ClarifyingGen">
      <bpmn:documentation>Message is ambiguous; generate a focused clarifying question instead of attempting a coaching response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">needsClarification == true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ClarifyGen_End" sourceRef="Task_ClarifyingGen" targetRef="Event_End_E10_Clarify">
      <bpmn:documentation>Clarifying question generated and sent; terminate at E10. User's reply will start a new turn.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_8_To_9" sourceRef="Call_Step8_Prompt" targetRef="Task_Step9_LLM">
      <bpmn:documentation>Prompt assembled; call primary LLM (5000ms hard cap).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_9_To_Merge" sourceRef="Task_Step9_LLM" targetRef="Gateway_LLM_Merge">
      <bpmn:documentation>LLM returned successfully; converge at merge gateway.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_Timeout" sourceRef="Error_LLM_Timeout" targetRef="Task_Fallback_FastModel">
      <bpmn:documentation>Timeout (&gt;5000ms); try fast-model fallback.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_Rate" sourceRef="Error_LLM_RateLimit" targetRef="Task_Fallback_FastModel">
      <bpmn:documentation>Rate limit (429); try fast-model fallback (different rate-limit pool).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_Filter" sourceRef="Error_LLM_Filter" targetRef="Task_Fallback_SafeResponse">
      <bpmn:documentation>Content filter rejection; do NOT retry with another model — issue is the input. Send templated safe response.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_Unavailable" sourceRef="Error_LLM_Unavailable" targetRef="Event_End_E11_Unavailable">
      <bpmn:documentation>LLM service unavailable (5xx, network); no fallback worth attempting; terminate at E11.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Fast_Merge" sourceRef="Task_Fallback_FastModel" targetRef="Gateway_LLM_Merge">
      <bpmn:documentation>Fast-model fallback succeeded; converge at merge (degraded flag set).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Safe_Merge" sourceRef="Task_Fallback_SafeResponse" targetRef="Gateway_LLM_Merge">
      <bpmn:documentation>Safe-response fallback applied; converge at merge (degraded flag set).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Merge_To_10" sourceRef="Gateway_LLM_Merge" targetRef="Call_Step10_QA">
      <bpmn:documentation>Candidate response (normal or fallback) ready; run Response Quality Check.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_10_To_GW4" sourceRef="Call_Step10_QA" targetRef="Gateway_Step10_Outcome">
      <bpmn:documentation>QA returned; route by outcome.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_QA_Approved" sourceRef="Gateway_Step10_Outcome" targetRef="Call_Step11_Delivery">
      <bpmn:documentation>Response approved; deliver via Process #11.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">qaOutcome == 'Approved' (default)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_QA_Crisis" sourceRef="Gateway_Step10_Outcome" targetRef="Call_CrisisSub">
      <bpmn:documentation>QA detected crisis content the LLM/Step 1 missed; divert to Crisis Handoff (second crisis-detection point).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">qaOutcome == 'CrisisEscalation'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_QA_Unavailable" sourceRef="Gateway_Step10_Outcome" targetRef="Event_End_E11_Unavailable">
      <bpmn:documentation>RQC infrastructure failure; terminate at E11.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">qaOutcome == 'ServiceUnavailable'</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_11_To_Split" sourceRef="Call_Step11_Delivery" targetRef="Gateway_Step12_PostSplit">
      <bpmn:documentation>Response delivered; fan out to 4 post-turn persistence branches (fail-open).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Post_12a" sourceRef="Gateway_Step12_PostSplit" targetRef="Task_Step12a_Log">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 1: log conversation turn.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Post_12b" sourceRef="Gateway_Step12_PostSplit" targetRef="Call_Step12b_MemoryWrite">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 2: write to long-term memory via Process #8.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Post_12c" sourceRef="Gateway_Step12_PostSplit" targetRef="Task_Step12c_Metrics">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 3: emit observability metrics.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Post_12d" sourceRef="Gateway_Step12_PostSplit" targetRef="Task_Step12d_Pattern">
      <bpmn:documentation>Branch 4: profile pattern detection.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12a_Join" sourceRef="Task_Step12a_Log" targetRef="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Log written successfully; converge at join.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12b_Join" sourceRef="Call_Step12b_MemoryWrite" targetRef="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Memory write succeeded; converge.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12c_Join" sourceRef="Task_Step12c_Metrics" targetRef="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Metrics emitted; converge.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12d_Join" sourceRef="Task_Step12d_Pattern" targetRef="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Pattern detection complete; converge.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_12a" sourceRef="Boundary_12a" targetRef="Call_Incident_PostTurn">
      <bpmn:documentation>Log write failed; route to incident (fail-open).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_12b" sourceRef="Boundary_12b" targetRef="Call_Incident_PostTurn">
      <bpmn:documentation>Memory write failed; route to incident (fail-open).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_12c" sourceRef="Boundary_12c" targetRef="Call_Incident_PostTurn">
      <bpmn:documentation>Metrics emission failed; route to incident (fail-open).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_12d" sourceRef="Boundary_12d" targetRef="Call_Incident_PostTurn">
      <bpmn:documentation>Pattern detection failed; route to incident (fail-open).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Incident_Join" sourceRef="Call_Incident_PostTurn" targetRef="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin">
      <bpmn:documentation>Incident logged asynchronously; converge at join (does NOT block other branches).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Join_To_13" sourceRef="Gateway_Step12_PostJoin" targetRef="Task_Step13_Continuation">
      <bpmn:documentation>All post-turn branches complete; evaluate session continuation.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_13_To_GW5" sourceRef="Task_Step13_Continuation" targetRef="Gateway_Step13_Close">
      <bpmn:documentation>Continuation decision; route by sessionAction and isDegraded.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_End_E1" sourceRef="Gateway_Step13_Close" targetRef="Event_End_E1_TurnCompleted">
      <bpmn:documentation>Standard happy path; session continues open; terminate at E1.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">sessionAction == 'KeepOpen' AND isDegraded == false (default)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_End_E3" sourceRef="Gateway_Step13_Close" targetRef="Event_End_E3_DegradedQuality">
      <bpmn:documentation>Turn was on a fallback path; close session by default for quality reasons; terminate at E3.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">isDegraded == true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_End_E2_Sig" sourceRef="Gateway_Step13_Close" targetRef="Event_SignalClose">
      <bpmn:documentation>Session close decided (explicit close keyword, max turns, or inactivity inferred); emit SessionClose signal.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">sessionAction == 'Close' AND isDegraded == false</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Sig_To_E2" sourceRef="Event_SignalClose" targetRef="Event_End_E2_TurnCompletedSessionClosed">
      <bpmn:documentation>SessionClose signal emitted to Process #6; terminate at E2.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
  </bpmn:process>
